<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU farm ministers to resume beef aid talks on Wed..</title>
<headline>EU farm ministers to resume beef aid talks on Wed..</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers suspended efforts to agree measures to cut beef production and to compensate farmers for losses caused by the mad cow crisis until Wednesday, EU officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;The meeting is due to resume at 9:00 (local/0800 GMT) with a new compromise from the Irish EU Presidency,&quot; an official said.</p>
<p>Farm ministers said on Tuesday a scheme to slaughter new born calves was unacceptable and the proposed aid was insufficient.</p>
<p>French Farm Minister Philippe Vasseur has called for 500 million Ecus of extra direct aid for livestock farmers.</p>
<p>But EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler has said the extra funds are not available in the EU farm budget.</p>
</text>
